{"type": "assistant_message", "timestamp": 1792653666.7294002, "id": "b494b0f15de0", "content": "", "tool_calls": [{"id": "call_00_zkfNsw640zLbKjdnEm7U1321", "name": "run_command", "arguments": "{\"command\": \"cat > /tmp/patch_yaw2.py <<'PYEOF'\\np = \\\"diff_env/target.py\\\"\\ns = open(p, encoding=\\\"utf-8\\\").read()\\nold = \\\"\\\"\\\"        armor_yaws = torch.atan2(world_normal[..., 1], world_normal[..., 0])\\\"\\\"\\\"\\nnew = \\\"\\\"\\\"        yaw_from_normal = torch.atan2(world_normal[..., 1], world_normal[..., 0])\\n        # a flat plate points straight up, so its yaw is undefined: fall back to\\n        # the yaw of the plate width axis (the legacy meaning of armour yaw)\\n        width_dir = world_rot[..., :, 0]\\n        yaw_from_width = torch.atan2(width_dir[..., 1], width_dir[..., 0])\\n        planar = torch.hypot(world_normal[..., 0], world_normal[..., 1])\\n        armor_yaws = torch.where(planar > 1e-3, yaw_from_normal, yaw_from_width)\\\"\\\"\\\"\\nassert old in s\\ns = s.replace(old, new, 1)\\nopen(p, \\\"w\\\", encoding=\\\"utf-8\\\").write(s)\\nprint(\\\"yaw fallback added\\\")\\nPYEOF\\npython3 /tmp/patch_yaw2.py && .venv/bin/python /tmp/check_env.py && .venv/bin/python scripts/visualize_target.py --test 2>&1 | tail -4\"}"}], "reasoning": "Legacy (horizontal, pitch=15) still gives [0, 1.571, -3.142, -1.571] = θ ✓ identical to before, so no behavior change for existing code. Vertical now gives the facing yaw = θ ✓.\n\nBut note for horizontal pitch=0 the normal is exactly +Z → atan2(0,0)=0 for all → degenerate. Edge case; acceptable (the normal is vertical so yaw is undefined). Maybe guard: if the normal is nearly vertical, fall back to the width axis? For legacy pitch=0 all yaws become 0, whereas before it was θ. That's a regression for the legacy baseline (armor_yaws less informative when plates are flat). Since the default pitch is 15°, it's fine; but to be safe and preserve the old semantics for the horizontal case, I could compute the yaw of the in-plane \"width\" axis for horizontal and normal for vertical? That reintroduces inconsistency.\n\nBetter: keep the normal-based yaw but for the degenerate case (|n_xy| tiny) fall back to the local X axis yaw. Implement:\n\n```python\n        planar = torch.hypot(world_normal[..., 0], world_normal[..., 1])\n        width_dir = world_rot[..., :, 0]\n        fallback = torch.atan2(width_dir[..., 1], width_dir[..., 0])\n        yaw_normal = torch.atan2(world_normal[..., 1], world_normal[..., 0])\n        armor_yaws = torch.where(planar > 1e-3, yaw_normal, fallback)\n```\nThis keeps pitch=0 horizontal returning θ (the width axis yaw) — matching the old behavior exactly, and uses the normal when meaningful.\n\nLet me add that. Then re-run and re-run the env check + the visualization test and regenerate images.\n\nAlso double check the `plate_orientation` docstring placement — the ArmorLayout docstring documents only plate_orientation; fine.\n\nOne more consideration: `TargetMotion.forward` docstring/README? None.\n\nLet me patch the degenerate fallback."}
{"type": "tool_call", "timestamp": 1792653666.7293699, "id": "1ded7222c41b", "name": "run_command", "arguments": "{\"command\": \"cat > /tmp/patch_yaw2.py <<'PYEOF'\\np = \\\"diff_env/target.py\\\"\\ns = open(p, encoding=\\\"utf-8\\\").read()\\nold = \\\"\\\"\\\"        armor_yaws = torch.atan2(world_normal[..., 1], world_normal[..., 0])\\\"\\\"\\\"\\nnew = \\\"\\\"\\\"        yaw_from_normal = torch.atan2(world_normal[..., 1], world_normal[..., 0])\\n        # a flat plate points straight up, so its yaw is undefined: fall back to\\n        # the yaw of the plate width axis (the legacy meaning of armour yaw)\\n        width_dir = world_rot[..., :, 0]\\n        yaw_from_width = torch.atan2(width_dir[..., 1], width_dir[..., 0])\\n        planar = torch.hypot(world_normal[..., 0], world_normal[..., 1])\\n        armor_yaws = torch.where(planar > 1e-3, yaw_from_normal, yaw_from_width)\\\"\\\"\\\"\\nassert old in s\\ns = s.replace(old, new, 1)\\nopen(p, \\\"w\\\", encoding=\\\"utf-8\\\").write(s)\\nprint(\\\"yaw fallback added\\\")\\nPYEOF\\npython3 /tmp/patch_yaw2.py && .venv/bin/python /tmp/check_env.py && .venv/bin/python scripts/visualize_target.py --test 2>&1 | tail -4\"}", "tool_call_id": "call_00_zkfNsw640zLbKjdnEm7U1321", "ui": {"group": null, "chip": "name", "summary": "", "preview": "command", "header": "", "form": "block", "body": "text", "collapse": "never", "highlight": "", "chrome": "", "mutates": true, "undo": false}, "path_arg": ""}
