{"type": "assistant_message", "timestamp": 1792654144.2716494, "id": "9307376f91e6", "content": "", "tool_calls": [{"id": "call_00_jQzl9esqpkplSUeNEz4P8329", "name": "run_command", "arguments": "{\"command\": \"cat > /tmp/patch_target.py <<\\\"PYEOF\\\"\\nimport io\\np = \\\"diff_env/target.py\\\"\\ns = open(p).read()\\n\\nold_param = '''        if armor_pitch is None:\\n            armor_pitch = torch.full(\\n                (bsz, n_armors), math.radians(15.0), device=device, dtype=radius.dtype\\n            )\\n        elif not isinstance(armor_pitch, torch.Tensor):\\n            armor_pitch = torch.full(\\n                (bsz, n_armors), float(armor_pitch), device=device, dtype=radius.dtype\\n            )\\n\\n'''\\nassert old_param in s\\ns = s.replace(old_param, \\\"\\\")\\n\\ns = s.replace('''        armor_pitch: torch.Tensor | None = None,\\n''', \\\"\\\")\\n\\nold_rot = '''        # upright plate: width (+X) tangential, height (+Y) up, normal (+Z)\\n        # radially outward and lifted by armor_pitch\\n        roll = torch.full_like(yaws, math.pi / 2)\\n        local_rotations = euler_to_rotmat(yaws + math.pi / 2, -armor_pitch, roll)'''\\nnew_rot = '''        # vertical armor: width tangential, height up, normal radial outward\\n        zeros = torch.zeros_like(yaws)\\n        half_pi = torch.full_like(yaws, math.pi / 2)\\n        local_rotations = euler_to_rotmat(yaws + half_pi, zeros, half_pi)'''\\nassert old_rot in s\\ns = s.replace(old_rot, new_rot)\\n\\nold_call = '''        local_pos, local_rot, corners_local = self.armor_layout(\\n            n_armors,\\n            radius,\\n            radius_offsets,\\n            height_offsets,\\n            params.get(\\\"armor_pitch\\\", None),\\n        )'''\\nnew_call = '''        local_pos, local_rot, corners_local = self.armor_layout(\\n            n_armors, radius, radius_offsets, height_offsets\\n        )'''\\nassert old_call in s\\ns = s.replace(old_call, new_call)\\nopen(p, \\\"w\\\").write(s)\\nprint(\\\"patched\\\")\\nPYEOF\\n.venv/bin/python /tmp/patch_target.py && python3 -c \\\"import ast; ast.parse(open('diff_env/target.py').read())\\\" && echo AST_OK && sed -n 84,125p diff_env/target.py\"}"}], "reasoning": "No consumers. So armor_pitch is entirely a visualization-session addition. The user now asks to keep only vertical default, original logic, no complex mode/strings — I think the right minimal target.py is:\n\n```python\nyaws = theta.unsqueeze(0)\nzeros = torch.zeros_like(yaws)\nlocal_rotations = euler_to_rotmat(yaws + math.pi / 2, zeros, torch.full_like(yaws, math.pi / 2))\n```\n\ni.e., vertical armor, no armor_pitch plumbing at all. And remove `armor_pitch` from the script (CLI --armor-pitch-deg) too? Hmm, but the summary of user requirements says \"只保留vertical作为默认值\" — that's about the plate_orientation mode. Removing the pitch param entirely matches \"不要加复杂的模式定义\" and \"过程中实际对问题没有改进的代码\". The armor_pitch wasn't part of the original env, and it doesn't change the vertical-ness except in-plane spin. But it does change the visualization subtly.\n\nHowever, hold on: perhaps the physical 15° tilt is desired to match real armor. Let me reconsider: can we get the tilt using the euler by applying pitch to yaw instead? The plate normal for vertical is horizontal; a \"pitch\" tilt of the plate could be represented as rotating the plate about the tangential axis, which in terms of the final world normal adds nz. Since the euler composition can't do it with local-axis ordering, one can build the plate from corners in a different local frame... but that's extra complexity, exactly what the user doesn't want.\n\nActually wait — maybe there IS a clean euler representation. The rotation we want: R_world_from_local = Rz(θ) * Ry(π/2 - p_as_tilt?) ... Let's revisit: We want columns:\nex → t = (-sinθ, cosθ, 0)   [tangential]\ney → h = (-sin p cosθ, -sin p sinθ, cos p)  [up, tilted]\nez → n = (cos p cosθ, cos p sinθ, sin p)  [outward, lifted]\n\nWe showed R = Rz(θ) * S where S columns (0,1,0), (-sin p,0,cos p), (cos p,0,sin p). Is S expressible as Ry(a)Rx(r)? We computed Ry(a)Rx(r) columns: (ca, 0, -sa), (sa sr, cr, ca sr), (sa cr, -sr, ca cr). Setting first column = (0,1,0) impossible. What about S = Ry(a)Rz(c)? euler doesn't have Rz in the middle-right... but euler has Rz as leftmost only.\n\nAlternatively represent rotation differently: R = Rz(θ) Rx(90) then tilt in world about tangential axis — but a single euler can't since the tilt axis depends on θ (it's the body-fixed x, which is after Rz). Actually euler Rz(θ) Ry(p) Rx(r): the Ry happens before Rz, i.e., about the y axis of the intermediate frame, which after Rz(θ) is the world direction Rz(θ) ey = (-sinθ, cosθ,0) = tangential! Wait! Order: R = Rz(θ) @ Ry(p) @ Rx(r). Applied to a vector v: first Rx(r), then Ry(p) about the fixed y axis of the frame *before* Rz — that frame's y axis is ey = (0,1,0) in the pre-Rz world; after Rz(θ), that axis becomes Rz(θ)ey = (-sinθ, cosθ, 0) = tangential ✓. So Ry(p) rotates the plate about the tangential axis — exactly the physical pitch tilt! But the problem is that the intermediate plate orientation before Ry is produced by Rx(r) only, and Rx(r) sends ez to (0,-sin r, cos r) — not radial. Then Ry(p) rotates that about y: (0,-sin r, cos r) → (sin p cos r, -sin r, cos p cos r). Then Rz(θ): (cosθ sin p cos r + sinθ sin r, sinθ sin p cos r - cosθ sin r, cos p cos r). For this to be horizontal radial (n = (cosθ, sinθ, 0)) we need cos p cos r = 0 → r = ±90° and sin p cos r = ±sin p... with r=90: cos r=0, sin r=1: n before Rz = (0,-1,0) → Rz → (sinθ, -cosθ, 0) = -radial. With r=-90: (0,1,0) → Rz → (-sinθ, cosθ,0) = tangential — wrong.\n\nRight, so with r=±90 the plate normal is in the tangential or -radial horizontal direction; Ry(p) then rotates it about y (tangential) out of the horizontal plane? Let's recompute with r=-90: Rx(-90) ez = (0, sin? ) Rx(-90) = [[1,0,0],[0,0,1],[0,-1,0]] applied to ez = (0,1,0). Ry(p)(0,1,0) = (0,1,0)? Ry doesn't affect y. Hmm I miscomputed: Ry(p) applied to (0,1,0) = (0,1,0) always. So normal after Ry is (0,1,0) — tangential after Rz. So the normal is horizontal tangential, i.e. the plate faces sideways (like a fan blade), not outward. So indeed impossible.\n\nOK so with `euler_to_rotmat` as-is, no pitch tilt; the formula I have produces vertical plates with in-plane rotation. Two choices:\n(a) accept vertical plates, remove armor_pitch plumbing, formula `euler_to_rotmat(yaws + math.pi/2, zeros, pi/2)`.\n(b) keep armor_pitch but it acts in-plane (weird, and misleading comment \"lifted by armor_pitch\").\n\nGiven user requirement \"按原来的逻辑写\" (write per the original logic) and \"不要加复杂\" — I think (a) is right: the plates are vertical, normal radial. But wait, does the user want the 15° tilt? The original env literally had `zeros` for pitch and roll: `euler_to_rotmat(yaws, zeros, zeros)`. armor_pitch wasn't in the original. It's an addition from the visualization process. So removing it aligns with \"过程中实际对问题没有改进的代码…删掉\".\n\nBut hmm: the summary says the user accepted \"diff_env 默认改为 vertical 会改变 corners/centers 数值（用户已同意只保留 vertical）\". That concerns the layout change, not pitch.\n\nLet me decide: Keep a single `armor_pitch`? No — remove it. Minimal original-style code:\n\n```python\n        yaws = theta.unsqueeze(0)\n        zeros = torch.zeros_like(yaws)\n        # upright armor: width tangential, height vertical, normal radial\n        local_rotations = euler_to_rotmat(yaws + math.pi / 2, zeros, math.pi / 2 + zeros)\n```\n\nHmm, euler_to_rotmat expects tensors; math.pi/2 + zeros gives tensor of π/2 shape (1,n) which broadcasts with yaws (1,n) fine (bsz=1 expand... wait yaws = theta.unsqueeze(0) shape (1,n), and bsz may be >1; r_eff handles bsz via radius.unsqueeze(-1) (bsz,1) broadcast with theta (n,), giving (bsz,n). Then corners computed with corners_local (4,3) → fine. local_rotations (1,n,3,3) broadcasts in einsum with body_rot (b,t,3,3): \"btik,bmkj->btmij\" needs m to match n: bmkj with m=n from local_rot (1,n,...) broadcasts to b? einsum doesn't broadcast leading dim of size 1? Actually torch.einsum does support broadcasting for dimensions with size 1. So (b,t,3,3) x (1,n,3,3) -> (b,t,n,3,3) works. Fine, but with bsz>1 it's better `yaws = theta.unsqueeze(0).expand(bsz, -1)` as currently. The diff already has `.expand(bsz, -1)`. Keep that (it's needed because radius offsets make bsz>1? theta is (n,) and r_eff (bsz,n), corners_local (4,3) → world_rot = einsum body_rot (b,t) x local_rot (1,n) — works with broadcast but expand is harmless and clearer).\n\nLet me now decide about the `zeros` shape: `zeros = torch.zeros_like(yaws)` then `euler_to_rotmat(yaws + math.pi / 2, zeros, zeros + math.pi / 2)`. Cleaner:\n\n```python\n        yaws = theta.unsqueeze(0).expand(bsz, -1)\n        zeros = torch.zeros_like(yaws)\n        # vertical armor: width tangential, height up, normal radial outward\n        local_rotations = euler_to_rotmat(yaws + math.pi / 2, zeros, zeros + math.pi / 2)\n```\n\nCheck: R = Rz(θ+90) Ry(0) Rx(90) = Rz(θ+90) Rx(90) ✓ (as derived: outward normal, width tangential, height up).\n\nVerify numerically after edit.\n\nThen remove armor_pitch from ArmorLayout signature & TargetMotion forwarding (restore original call `self.armor_layout(n_armors, radius, radius_offsets, height_offsets)`), remove `--armor-pitch-deg` from the script and the make_scene param, and self-test assert |nz| ≈ 0 (vertical plate normals are horizontal): `assert np.abs(normals[0, :, 2]).max() < 1e-6`. And also assert extent: height 0.06 vertical, width tangential: for θ=0 plate, corner extents (x: 0, y: 0.12, z: 0.06). That's a good geometric check.\n\nHmm wait, but maybe keeping a small armor pitch is nice for realistic rendering. Yet the user explicitly wants simple original logic. The original had `euler_to_rotmat(yaws, zeros, zeros)`: no pitch. So mirror that: `euler_to_rotmat(yaws + pi/2, zeros, zeros + pi/2)`.\n\nHmm, but is \"原来的逻辑\" perhaps meaning \"keep the original computation of corners/centers using the body rotation and offsets\" — i.e., don't add modes. Removing armor_pitch simplifies further, consistent with \"删掉没改进的代码\".\n\nBut hold on: changing target.py again changes center values? No—centers depend on local_positions, which depend on radius/offsets only, not rotations. Corners change only in orientation. armor_yaws: with normal = radial outward, armor_yaws = θ ✓.\n\nBut there's a subtlety: the self-test needs `armor_pitch_deg` no more. Remove from script args and note.\n\nAlso the docstring/README may mention? grep.\n\nLet me now edit target.py via a small python patch script (avoid apostrophes). Replace lines:\n\n```\n        yaws = theta.unsqueeze(0).expand(bsz, -1)\n        # upright plate: width (+X) tangential, height (+Y) up, normal (+Z)\n        # radially outward and lifted by armor_pitch\n        roll = torch.full_like(yaws, math.pi / 2)\n        local_rotations = euler_to_rotmat(yaws + math.pi / 2, -armor_pitch, roll)\n```\nwith\n```\n        yaws = theta.unsqueeze(0).expand(bsz, -1)\n        zeros = torch.zeros_like(yaws)\n        # vertical armor: width tangential, height up, normal radial outward\n        local_rotations = euler_to_rotmat(yaws + math.pi / 2, zeros, zeros + math.pi / 2)\n```\n\nAnd remove the armor_pitch parameter block in ArmorLayout.forward, and the forwarding param.\n\nWait, but is `zeros + math.pi / 2` fine? yes tensor.\n\nActually maybe cleaner to define `half_pi = torch.full_like(yaws, math.pi / 2)` and use `euler_to_rotmat(yaws + half_pi, zeros, half_pi)`.\n\nNow, does the summary's verification \"pitch=0 时 extent (0, 0.12, 0.06)\" hold with this? Yes, same as before at pitch=0. And the previous session's rendered image used pitch=-15 in Ry slot (in-plane spin) — my new version removes that spin, so the rendered image changes slightly (rectangles no longer tilted in their own plane). Fine, and arguably cleaner.\n\nWait, actually maybe I should double check the plate direction: with θ range 0,90,180,270 for n_armors=4. θ=0 → normal +X (toward body's... at position (radius,0)), i.e., outward +X = away from body center. At θ=0, the plate sits at +X side of the body, normal +X pointing away from body, i.e., facing forward — correct for armor at the front. ✓\n\nNow the self-test expectations at t=0 with body at (3,0,0.5), θ: 0, 90, 180, 270. Plates at body + R(body)·(r cosθ, r sinθ, h_off). Body yaw at t=0? yaw_0 param maybe pi? Let me check BodyMotion default params for \"complex\" and whether the test expectations (nearest plate faces camera) hold — previously it passed with the earlier formula, and vertical normals are the same at pitch=0? At pitch=15 (in-plane rotation), normal was still radial (computed nz=0 earlier). So facing geometry identical. Great, the self-test should still pass except the nz assertion which I'll change.\n\nAlso the projected-size assertion: v extent bound `cam.fy * armor_height / depth * 1.05 + 2` — with plate upright, v extent ≈ fy*0.06/depth ≈ 17.8 px, bound 18.7. Fine. u extent ≈ fx*0.12/depth.\n\nLet me now apply the target.py edits.\n\nAlso remove from visualize script: --armor-pitch-deg, armor_pitch in make_scene, note string, self-test nz assert → horizontal check.\n\nLet me do the target.py patch first."}
{"type": "tool_call", "timestamp": 1792654144.2716112, "id": "30c41d55c46c", "name": "run_command", "arguments": "{\"command\": \"cat > /tmp/patch_target.py <<\\\"PYEOF\\\"\\nimport io\\np = \\\"diff_env/target.py\\\"\\ns = open(p).read()\\n\\nold_param = '''        if armor_pitch is None:\\n            armor_pitch = torch.full(\\n                (bsz, n_armors), math.radians(15.0), device=device, dtype=radius.dtype\\n            )\\n        elif not isinstance(armor_pitch, torch.Tensor):\\n            armor_pitch = torch.full(\\n                (bsz, n_armors), float(armor_pitch), device=device, dtype=radius.dtype\\n            )\\n\\n'''\\nassert old_param in s\\ns = s.replace(old_param, \\\"\\\")\\n\\ns = s.replace('''        armor_pitch: torch.Tensor | None = None,\\n''', \\\"\\\")\\n\\nold_rot = '''        # upright plate: width (+X) tangential, height (+Y) up, normal (+Z)\\n        # radially outward and lifted by armor_pitch\\n        roll = torch.full_like(yaws, math.pi / 2)\\n        local_rotations = euler_to_rotmat(yaws + math.pi / 2, -armor_pitch, roll)'''\\nnew_rot = '''        # vertical armor: width tangential, height up, normal radial outward\\n        zeros = torch.zeros_like(yaws)\\n        half_pi = torch.full_like(yaws, math.pi / 2)\\n        local_rotations = euler_to_rotmat(yaws + half_pi, zeros, half_pi)'''\\nassert old_rot in s\\ns = s.replace(old_rot, new_rot)\\n\\nold_call = '''        local_pos, local_rot, corners_local = self.armor_layout(\\n            n_armors,\\n            radius,\\n            radius_offsets,\\n            height_offsets,\\n            params.get(\\\"armor_pitch\\\", None),\\n        )'''\\nnew_call = '''        local_pos, local_rot, corners_local = self.armor_layout(\\n            n_armors, radius, radius_offsets, height_offsets\\n        )'''\\nassert old_call in s\\ns = s.replace(old_call, new_call)\\nopen(p, \\\"w\\\").write(s)\\nprint(\\\"patched\\\")\\nPYEOF\\n.venv/bin/python /tmp/patch_target.py && python3 -c \\\"import ast; ast.parse(open('diff_env/target.py').read())\\\" && echo AST_OK && sed -n 84,125p diff_env/target.py\"}", "tool_call_id": "call_00_jQzl9esqpkplSUeNEz4P8329", "ui": {"group": null, "chip": "name", "summary": "", "preview": "command", "header": "", "form": "block", "body": "text", "collapse": "never", "highlight": "", "chrome": "", "mutates": true, "undo": false}, "path_arg": ""}
{"type": "tool_result", "timestamp": 1792654144.36325, "id": "999f2cfdd80a", "tool_call_id": "call_00_jQzl9esqpkplSUeNEz4P8329", "content": "OK: command succeeded\nstdout:\npatched\nAST_OK\n        self.armor_height = armor_height\n\n    def forward(\n        self,\n        n_armors: int,\n        radius: torch.Tensor,\n        radius_offsets: torch.Tensor | None = None,\n        height_offsets: torch.Tensor | None = None,\n    ):\n        device = radius.device\n        bsz = radius.shape[0]\n\n        if radius_offsets is None:\n            radius_offsets = torch.zeros(\n                bsz, n_armors, device=device, dtype=radius.dtype\n            )\n        if height_offsets is None:\n            height_offsets = torch.zeros(\n                bsz, n_armors, device=device, dtype=radius.dtype\n            )\n        theta = (\n            torch.arange(n_armors, device=device, dtype=radius.dtype)\n            * 2\n            * math.pi\n            / n_armors\n        )\n\n        r_eff = radius.unsqueeze(-1) + radius_offsets\n        local_x = r_eff * torch.cos(theta)\n        local_y = r_eff * torch.sin(theta)\n        local_z = height_offsets\n        local_positions = torch.stack([local_x, local_y, local_z], dim=-1)\n\n        yaws = theta.unsqueeze(0).expand(bsz, -1)\n        # vertical armor: width tangential, height up, normal radial outward\n        zeros = torch.zeros_like(yaws)\n        half_pi = torch.full_like(yaws, math.pi / 2)\n        local_rotations = euler_to_rotmat(yaws + half_pi, zeros, half_pi)\n\n        w2 = self.armor_width / 2\n        h2 = self.armor_height / 2\n        corners_local = torch.tensor(\n", "is_error": false, "diff": ""}
