{"type": "assistant_message", "timestamp": 1792656344.4526231, "id": "330dade9146e", "content": "", "tool_calls": [{"id": "call_00_1UkpmzIg3uaKq7UMaBL69970", "name": "run_command", "arguments": "{\"command\": \"cat > /tmp/ascii_frames.py <<\\\"PYEOF\\\"\\nimport sys\\nsys.path.insert(0, \\\".\\\")\\nimport numpy as np\\nfrom PIL import Image\\nfrom scripts.visualize_target import AXIS_COLORS\\n\\na = np.asarray(Image.open(\\\"scripts/target_vis.png\\\").convert(\\\"RGB\\\")).astype(int)\\nh, w = a.shape[:2]\\ncols = np.array([[int(c[i:i + 2], 16) for i in (1, 3, 5)] for c in AXIS_COLORS])\\ndist = np.abs(a[:, :, None, :] - cols[None, None]).sum(-1)\\nbest, ok = dist.argmin(-1), dist.min(-1) < 40\\npanels = {\\\"left\\\": (0, w // 3), \\\"mid\\\": (w // 3, 2 * w // 3), \\\"right\\\": (2 * w // 3, w)}\\nchars = \\\"XYZ\\\"\\nfor name, (xa, xb) in panels.items():\\n    sub = np.zeros_like(ok)\\n    sub[:, xa:xb] = ok[:, xa:xb]\\n    ys, xs = np.where(sub)\\n    print(name, \\\"axis-coloured px:\\\", len(xs))\\n    if not len(xs):\\n        continue\\n    x0, x1, y0, y1 = xs.min(), xs.max() + 1, ys.min(), ys.max() + 1\\n    for iy in range(16):\\n        row = \\\"\\\"\\n        for ix in range(56):\\n            ya, yb = y0 + (y1 - y0) * iy // 16, y0 + (y1 - y0) * (iy + 1) // 16\\n            ba, bb = x0 + (x1 - x0) * ix // 56, x0 + (x1 - x0) * (ix + 1) // 56\\n            block = sub[ya:yb, ba:bb]\\n            row += \\\".\\\" if not block.any() else chars[np.bincount(best[ya:yb, ba:bb][block]).argmax()]\\n        print(row)\\n    print()\\nPYEOF\\n.venv/bin/python /tmp/ascii_frames.py\"}"}], "reasoning": "The patch script has `yaws + half_pi`, and target.py mtime is 16:02:41 which matches add_rot.py's mtime (16:02:40.958) — i.e., the file was last written by add_rot.py at 16:02:41. So add_rot.py wrote the file, and its content... did add_rot.py alter the rotation? Let me view add_rot.py fully — I wrote:\n\n```python\np = \"diff_env/target.py\"\ns = open(p).read()\no